  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.0.0 - Audit fixes and corrected API contracts.\n\nBREAKING CHANGES:\n- Removed .NET 6/7 targets and support; .NET applications must target .NET 8 or later\n- SearchMessages now returns PagedResponse<MessageSearchItem>; removed the extra MessageSearchResults wrapper\n- DelegationMessage.Trackings now uses Models.Request.Tracking (label/value)\n- HttpLoggingHandler was removed because it exposed credentials and fax contents\n- Removed ContactAddressRequest.NotifyOnSend, NotifyOnReceive and IsPrimary; use contact-level notification settings\n\nFIXES:\n- Atomically publish one token snapshot; expiry and bearer credentials cannot come from different refreshes\n- Correct folder/user moves, route search, contact addresses, user creation, and message search request fields\n- Send maxResult for pagination; add pagination to user searches\n- Map user-search, contact-creation, and pagination response fields explicitly\n- Preserve named search-filter encoding and the bool IncludeSubdomain API until numeric meanings are verified on a live server\n- Remove duplicated factory validation; keep constructor validation\n- Use framework-provided HTTP assemblies instead of the legacy System.Net.Http NuGet package\n- On .NET 8+, the client-owned HttpClient recycles pooled connections every 2 minutes so long-lived clients follow DNS changes\n\nVALIDATION AND COMPATIBILITY:\n- Offline request, parsing, authentication, cancellation, and HttpClient ownership regression tests\n- Live tests require explicit opt-in, a dedicated account, and a configured recipient; only test-created messages are modified\n- Verified latest stable direct dependencies, including System.Text.Json 10.0.12, Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk 18.10.1 and xunit.runner.visualstudio 4.0.0\n- Added net9.0 and net10.0 targets; offline tests run on .NET 8, 9 and 10\n- Retained .NET Framework 4.7, 4.7.1, 4.7.2 and 4.8 targets; Microsoft lists these versions as Active, subject to the host Windows lifecycle\n- Response fixtures are synthetic; live FaxCore response compatibility still requires integration verification\n- Numeric search-filter mappings and server acceptance of named filters remain unverified; no live credentials were configured during validation",
